WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.540
To understand ratios,

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.040
you just need to understand the simple story!

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.700
Gaurav and Jay used to receive chocolates

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.860
from a mysterious magic hand every day.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.640
But the magic hand was a little biased towards Jay.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.560
Every time it gave two chocolates to Gaurav,

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.740
it gave three to Jay.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.400
Two to Gaurav and three to Jay.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.580
Nobody knew why!

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.000
Of course Jay did not complain.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.420
So the ratio of the number of chocolates Gaurav

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.740
got to the number of chocolates Jay got

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.640
is written as 2 colon 3.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.960
Or 2 divided by 3.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.680
This can be read as 2 is to 3.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.580
We are basically comparing the number of chocolates.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.140
Gaurav got to the number of chocolates Jay got.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.740
This went on for quite a few days.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.560
So every time the magic hand gave two chocolates to Gaurav

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.460
it gave 3 chocolates to Jay.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.620
Now let's count the total number of chocolates each of them have.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:07.380
Gaurav has 4 and Jay has 6.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.720
The ratio now becomes 4 by 6.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.080
The magic hand again gives Gaurav of 2 chocolates,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.480
and Jay 3 chocolates.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:19.940
Now the total number of chocolates with Gaurav is 6

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.560
and the total number of chocolates with Jay is 9.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.540
So the ratio becomes 6 by 9.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:31.580
Both these ratios when simplified will give us 2 by 3.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:35.480
In every case the ratio has remained the same.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.220
What does this mean?

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.320
If we multiply 2 with 2 and 3 also with 2

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.620
we get 4 by 6.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:49.720
If we multiply 2 with 3 and 3 with 3, we will get 6 by 9.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.820
And similarly, if you multiply 2 with 4 and 3 with 4,

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:59.920
we will get 8 by 12 which is again equivalent to 2 by 3.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:04.480
So all the three ratios are equal to 2 by 3.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.220
What does all this mean?

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.860
It means that if the ratio of two quantities is 2 by 3,

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.440
then the quantities will be multiples of 2

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.100
and multiples of 3 respectively

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.720
and not necessarily just two and three.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.800
A few students have this confusion

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.940
that the ratio of two by three

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.360
will mean Gaurav has just two chocolates,

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.680
and jay just three chocolates.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.300
If the ratio is 2 by 3

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:36.820
then the quantities will be in the form of 2x and 3x,

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.400
where 2x and 3x are multiples of 2 and 3.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:45.480
So ratio is basically a comparison of quantities.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.460
But there is a bit more to comparison of quantities.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.600
We see that next.

